  "text": {
    "intro": "The preserves tent is the most competitive building at the show, and the only one with a locked door.\nFive entrants are involved. Determine each entrant's price, preserve and ingredient.\n- **Entrant**: Stanislaw, Rafferty, Harriet, Drusilla and Bernadette.\n- **Price** (listed from cheaper to dearer): $3, $5, $7, $9 and $11.\n- **Preserve**: green walnut pickle; rosehip syrup; medlar jam; sloe and apple butter; and quince jelly.\n- **Secret ingredient**: nothing whatsoever, orange zest, star anise, black pepper and a splash of gin.\nEvery entrant has a different price, preserve and ingredient, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The entrant who adds a splash of gin charges $3.",
      "The entrant who enters rosehip syrup does not charge $5. Stanislaw is exactly one price step cheaper than $5, with no price in between.",
      "The entrant who adds nothing whatsoever is exactly one price step cheaper than $11, with no price in between.",
      "Drusilla falls somewhere between the entrant who enters sloe and apple butter and $3 in price order.",
      "Harriet and the entrant who adds orange zest are exactly one price step apart in price order, in one direction or the other.",
      "Rafferty is exactly one price step cheaper than the entrant who enters medlar jam, with no price in between.",
      "The entrant who enters medlar jam is exactly one price step cheaper than the entrant who adds orange zest, with no price in between.",
      "The entrant who enters quince jelly falls somewhere between Drusilla and Harriet in price order.",
      "The entrant who enters quince jelly and the entrant who adds star anise are exactly one price step apart in price order, in one direction or the other."
